Package: lindos-kernel
Version: 1.0.0
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), lindos-core
Recommends: scx-scheds
Suggests: lindos-tune
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Lindos-tuned kernel recipe, boot integration and runtime CLI
 The Lindos-tuned Linux kernel (ntsync, sched_ext, 1000 Hz + full preempt,
 MGLRU, zram/zswap, BBR, tuned kconfig).  This package ships everything
 *except* the compiled kernel image, which is a build artifact produced on a
 Linux host by build/kernel/build-kernel.sh and never committed.
 .
 It provides the single sources of truth for the kernel config fragment and
 feature manifest (/usr/share/lindos/kernel/), a conservative, reversible GRUB
 cmdline drop-in (/etc/default/grub.d/50-lindos.cfg, marker-fenced), and the
 /usr/bin/lindos-kernel command-line tool which reads the running kernel for
 the Lindos performance features, manages the cmdline drop-in and drives the
 out-of-tree build recipe.  Reading never needs root; mutating actions print
 the exact pkexec/update-grub command instead of calling sudo themselves.
